      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T09:15:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think what you want here is:\n1. Don\u0027t affect CRAS call\n2. If there is a `CallState::Incoming | CallState::Dialing | CallState::Alerting` call, remove it and set the phone state back to Idle\n3. If 2 is not true (*) and there is a `CallState::Active`, remove it and `self.phone_state.num_active -\u003d 1`\n4. When there is any phone state change, returns true so the caller would send out a phone state change\n\n*: Before I assert that there is exactly one incoming/dialing/alerting/active call after the match statement, but that may not be true anymore after this feature.\n\nI don\u0027t understand why you `c.state \u003d CallState::Idle` and then remove them immediately (using retain). At least the snippet can be revised to:\n```suggestion\n        self.call_list.retain(|c| match c.source {\n            CallSource::CRAS \u003d\u003e true,\n            CallSource::HID \u003d\u003e {\n                if c.state \u003d\u003d CallState::Active {\n                    self.phone_state.num_active -\u003d 1;\n                }\n                false\n            }\n        });\n        if self.phone_state.num_active \u003d\u003d 0 {\n            self.phone_state.state \u003d CallState::Idle;\n        }\n        // However, we shouldn\u0027t always return true\n```\n\nAgain please note that this code removes all HID calls, while I remember that we are going to support answering a call during a meeting? @whalechang@google.com please suggest.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1736,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1759,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "9263b4ca5f23926c0f83c506319ff31f2550d580",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6547bec3_1b45fcb6",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
