        "id": 2012120
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-01T07:52:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is possible to answer calls during a meeting. However, there should only be one active call at a time. When the user answers a new call, the old call should be hung up. This will depend on the implementation of the application. For example, on Android, the meeting session will end if the user answers a new call.\n\n\nIf the application does not behave in this way, it is not possible to know which call to hang up. This is because the UHID does not pass any information about the call, only a boolean value indicating whether the current call is hung up or not.\n\nIn that case, I think it is not that bad to simply end all the call.",
      "parentUuid": "283b512b_4b37d352",
